.TH UWCC-NVIDIA 1 "October 2026" "UWCC 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uwcc-nvidia, uwcc-nvidia-setup \- private NVIDIA runtime for UWCC
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uwcc-nvidia-setup
.RI [ --yes ]
.br
.B uwcc-nvidia
.RI [ UWCC-arguments ]
.br
.B uwcc-nvidia model-tools
.RI [ model-tool-arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The setup command creates a user-owned virtual environment, downloads pinned
ONNX Runtime GPU 1.31.0 with CUDA/cuDNN libraries from PyPI, and checks actual
CUDA inference. Run it as your desktop user, without sudo. Downloads may total
several gigabytes. A compatible NVIDIA GPU and driver must already be installed.
.PP
The launcher validates the environment and runs the apt-managed UWCC application
using its Python interpreter. It refuses to launch if CUDA validation fails;
the regular uwcc command remains available for CPU execution.
.PP
The model-tools subcommand runs model preparation or GPU validation inside
the NVIDIA environment. It requires the uwcc-model-tools package.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --yes
Accept the setup download without an interactive prompt.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B UWCC_NVIDIA_ENV
Override the private environment directory. By default it is located under
$XDG_DATA_HOME/uwcc/runtimes with the Python ABI and ONNX Runtime version in
the directory name. XDG_DATA_HOME defaults to ~/.local/share.
.PP
Models use UWCC_MODEL_DIR or the normal UWCC user data directory. Neither
setup nor launch installs drivers or downloads weights.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR uwcc (1),
.BR uwcc-models (1)
